<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Shervashidze</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chachba</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Shervashidze, called Chachba in Abkhaz, were the princely family that ruled Abkhazia from the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> until 1864. Originally governors under the Georgian kings and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-dadiani">Dadiani of Mingrelia</a>, they became independent princes as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> broke up, and many converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> under Ottoman influence. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keleshbey-chachba">Keleshbey Chachba</a> strengthened their rule around 1800, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> ended it by deposing the last prince, Mikhail, in 1864.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-shervashidze.jpg" alt="House of Shervashidze" width="320" height="434" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: I.V Borisov - painted the coat of arms · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_Arms_of_the_Sharvashidze.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
